  "hypotheses": [
    "Per-gate restoration increases routing SWAPs.",
    "Final restoration is unnecessary when a final permutation is allowed.",
    "Public nondefault routing can improve counts but is not guaranteed to do so.",
    "Post-basis optimization and one-qubit basis choices may affect the measured pipeline.",
    "Native SWAP lowering and local two-qubit block optimization may leave residual overhead."
  ],
